>
>
> # Print tree to table
> prt(tr)
> prt(t): root=25
>
> [1] "prt(t): root=25\n"
> Error: evaluation nested too deeply: infinite recursion / options(expressions=)?
> ==============================
>
> This is why I like the full example script, even though it seems tedious -- these kinds of issues are much more obvious when the files are read in directly, rather than deep inside some BioGeoBEARS function.
>
> I don't know what the issue was, but FigTree read the newick file OK, so I ordered the nodes in FigTree and saved back out to Newick, and the newick file tree2.newick works.
>
>
> 6. Distances file
>
> * Probably just add a blank line after "END" to get rid of the warning.
